# Language

Reports and replies to the owner in chat are in Japanese: the end-of-turn report, answers to questions, and the questions put to the owner. Identifiers, file names, and quoted English text stay as they are.

## English

- Code: identifiers, XML docs, inline comments, exception and diagnostic messages (including source generator and analyzer diagnostics), `BannedSymbols.txt` messages.
- Tests: method names, `summary` and `remarks`, assertion and skip messages.
- Commit subjects, PR titles, the `type` and `scope` of both, and the PR template headings.
- `.cursor/rules/`, `.agents/skills/` written in this repository, `.github/` templates, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `SECURITY.md`, `CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`.
- `README.md` and package descriptions. `README.md` is the source of truth; `README.ja.md` is its Japanese translation and changes in the same PR.

Before writing XML docs or comments, read `.agents/skills/english-writing/SKILL.md`. When a review corrects wording, add the general rule there in the same change.

## Japanese is allowed

- The design and the documents next to it: `docs/design.ja.md` (the canonical spec), `docs/design-decisions.md`, `docs/roadmap.md`, `docs/conventions.md`. An English design is a roadmap row, not kept in sync before then.
- `README.ja.md`.
- Issue bodies, PR bodies (below the English headings), commit bodies, and review replies.
- Test data that is Japanese on purpose (a Unicode string bound as a parameter). Explain it in an English comment next to it.
- `.agents/skills/natural-japanese/` (vendored; do not edit).

## Japanese writing

Japanese documents use plain form (常体), keep identifiers, SQL, and code in English, and are checked with `.agents/skills/natural-japanese/` before they are published.
